      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Baton Rouge, Gross‑Tete, and Opelousas Railroad, chartered in 1853, established a terminal near Port Allen, turning the village into a transportation hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Port_Allen,_Louisiana",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Port Allen’s Mississippi Riverfront Development offers a sweeping view of the river and Baton Rouge, making it a scenic spot for locals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Allen%2C_Louisiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Long before settlers, the area that is now Port Allen hosted mound‑building cultures of indigenous peoples along the west bank of the Mississippi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
